Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below are the columns (from the three datasets we will actually query) together with the role they will play and the typical conditions we will need:

•  bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_hiring  
  – `workforce`: choose `"overall"`  
  – `report_year`: choose `2021`  
  – `race_asian`, `race_black`, `race_hispanic_latinx`, `race_white`: racial shares of hires  
  – `gender_us_women`, `gender_us_men`: U.S‑based gender shares of hires  

•  bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation  
  – (identical column names / meanings as above) – filter to `workforce = 'overall'` and `report_year = 2021`  

•  bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18  
  – `year`: choose `2021`  
  – `industry`: choose exactly  
      • “Computer systems design and related services”  
      • “Internet publishing and broadcasting and web search portals”  
  – `percent_women` (compute men as `1‑percent_women`)  
  – `percent_white`, `percent_black_or_african_american`, `percent_asian`, `percent_hispanic_or_latino`  

With those columns in mind, here are ten exploratory → increasingly complex SQL statements (all limited to 20 rows) to understand / combine the needed pieces.

```sql
-- 1. Show which workforce buckets exist in Google hiring for 2021
SELECT DISTINCT workforce
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_hiring`
WHERE report_year = 2021
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Google OVERALL hiring, 2021 – raw racial & gender shares
SELECT workforce,
       race_asian,
       race_black,
       race_hispanic_latinx,
       race_white,
       gender_us_women,
       gender_us_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_hiring`
WHERE workforce = 'overall'
  AND report_year = 2021
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Google OVERALL representation, 2021 – raw racial & gender shares
SELECT workforce,
       race_asian,
       race_black,
       race_hispanic_latinx,
       race_white,
       gender_us_women,
       gender_us_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation`
WHERE workforce = 'overall'
  AND report_year = 2021
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Distinct tech‑related industries in BLS CPSAAT table for 2021 (quick check)
SELECT DISTINCT industry
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
WHERE year = 2021
  AND LOWER(industry) LIKE '%computer systems design%'
  OR  LOWER(industry) LIKE '%internet publishing%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. BLS – Computer systems design & related services (2021) racial / gender
SELECT industry,
       percent_white,
       percent_black_or_african_american AS percent_black,
       percent_asian,
       percent_hispanic_or_latino AS percent_hispanic_latinx,
       percent_women,
       1 - percent_women AS percent_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
WHERE year = 2021
  AND industry = 'Computer systems design and related services'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. BLS – Internet publishing & web search portals (2021) racial / gender
SELECT industry,
       percent_white,
       percent_black_or_african_american AS percent_black,
       percent_asian,
       percent_hispanic_or_latino AS percent_hispanic_latinx,
       percent_women,
       1 - percent_women AS percent_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
WHERE year = 2021
  AND industry = 'Internet publishing and broadcasting and web search portals'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Combine the two BLS tech industries for 2021 in one result
SELECT 'BLS – Tech Sector' AS source,
       industry,
       percent_white,
       percent_black_or_african_american AS percent_black,
       percent_asian,
       percent_hispanic_or_latino AS percent_hispanic_latinx,
       percent_women,
       1 - percent_women AS percent_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
WHERE year = 2021
  AND industry IN ('Computer systems design and related services',
                   'Internet publishing and broadcasting and web search portals')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Google hiring vs. representation side‑by‑side (simple UNION)
SELECT 'Google Hiring' AS source, race_asian, race_black, race_hispanic_latinx, race_white,
       gender_us_women, gender_us_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_hiring`
WHERE workforce = 'overall' AND report_year = 2021
UNION ALL
SELECT 'Google Representation' AS source, race_asian, race_black, race_hispanic_latinx, race_white,
       gender_us_women, gender_us_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation`
WHERE workforce = 'overall' AND report_year = 2021
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Full three‑way UNION (Google hiring, Google representation, BLS tech)
SELECT 'Google Hiring' AS source, race_asian, race_black, race_hispanic_latinx, race_white,
       gender_us_women AS percent_women, gender_us_men AS percent_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_hiring`
WHERE workforce = 'overall' AND report_year = 2021
UNION ALL
SELECT 'Google Representation', race_asian, race_black, race_hispanic_latinx, race_white,
       gender_us_women, gender_us_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation`
WHERE workforce = 'overall' AND report_year = 2021
UNION ALL
SELECT CONCAT('BLS – ', industry) AS source,
       percent_asian   AS race_asian,
       percent_black_or_african_american AS race_black,
       percent_hispanic_or_latino AS race_hispanic_latinx,
       percent_white   AS race_white,
       percent_women   AS percent_women,
       1 - percent_women AS percent_men
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
WHERE year = 2021
  AND industry IN ('Computer systems design and related services',
                   'Internet publishing and broadcasting and web search portals')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Pivot‑style summary: show all six shares in columns for each source
WITH google_hiring AS (
  SELECT 'Google Hiring' AS source,
         race_asian, race_black, race_hispanic_latinx, race_white,
         gender_us_women AS percent_women,
         gender_us_men   AS percent_men
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_hiring`
  WHERE workforce = 'overall' AND report_year = 2021
),
google_repr AS (
  SELECT 'Google Representation' AS source,
         race_asian, race_black, race_hispanic_latinx, race_white,
         gender_us_women AS percent_women,
         gender_us_men   AS percent_men
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation`
  WHERE workforce = 'overall' AND report_year = 2021
),
bls_tech AS (
  SELECT CONCAT('BLS – ', industry) AS source,
         percent_asian   AS race_asian,
         percent_black_or_african_american AS race_black,
         percent_hispanic_or_latino AS race_hispanic_latinx,
         percent_white   AS race_white,
         percent_women   AS percent_women,
         1 - percent_women AS percent_men
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.bls.cpsaat18`
  WHERE year = 2021
    AND industry IN ('Computer systems design and related services',
                     'Internet publishing and broadcasting and web search portals')
)
SELECT *
FROM google_hiring
UNION ALL
SELECT * FROM google_repr
UNION ALL
SELECT * FROM bls_tech
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries progress from basic inspection of values all the way to a concise 2021 comparison table that can directly feed your combined racial & gender distribution report.
